      "Explains why a prompt instruction alone is an incomplete fix: it can reduce SOME hallucination (nudging the model toward hedging/uncertainty language in genuinely ambiguous cases) but can't give the model actual knowledge it lacks, or a true mechanism for verifying its own output against reality -- a prompt instruction changes STYLE/behavior tendencies, not the model's fundamental lack of a ground-truth-checking capability.",
